## PART B — THE ARTEFACT

### B1 ALREADY BUILT — (a) the post-second-pass purge exists, twice, and is **guarded off**

EDIT 1 is not a new mechanism. It is already written into this stage's own parent recipe:

* `tools/recipes/build_d1_m3a3.py:1436-1437` — `nodes_now = node_census(...)` ; `purge_junk(nodes_now, "%s re-connect" % tag, hints)`, inside `phase_second_pass`;
* `tools/recipes/build_d1_m3a2.py:965-966` — the identical pair.

Both sit under `if not rec["idempotent"]:` (`build_d1_m3a3.py:1432`, `build_d1_m3a2.py:961`), i.e. they fire only when `wire_delta != 0` — which the second pass is designed never to be. That guard is **why** the current bed carries a junk node, and the new unconditional `s.junk_purge("rowD SECOND PASS", …)` (`stage_d1_m3a3_rowD.py:85`) silently overturns it without saying so. The correction is sound (the node is minted by the *call*, not by the wire delta — `stagekit.py:467-468`), but it is a reversal of an existing written decision and should be recorded as one, in the two places that still hold the old rule.

### B2 ALREADY FAILED — no finding

The 15:36:12 run failed exactly one gate, D7, and both edits address that record rather than repeat it. Nothing here re-runs a build whose cause of failure is unaddressed.

### B3 HELPER EXISTS — (c) the keyed-table comparison shape exists, and the two-line comprehension drops its value half

`tools/recipes/stage_d1_s2.py:658-674` `compare_subvi_tables` (lifted verbatim from `stage_d1_s1.py:408-427`) plus `log_table_diff:677-694` is this project's existing answer to *"this table must equal the reference minus exactly the predicted delta"*: it keys rows and reports **missing / extra / changed**, where `changed` = same key, different VALUE.

D7's `key = (i, name, is_source, term_state(t))` (`stage_d1_m3a3_rowD.py:92`) folds the value into the key and keeps no value at all, so a terminal that stays WIRED while the **wire identity** under it changes is invisible to the gate — precisely the class of silent substitution the c87 review's §2(a) says this run cannot attribute (`archive/peer/2026-09-22-c87-rowd-d7-termcount.md:127`). The rows carry `wire` (`build_d1_m3a1.py:507-510`, printed at `:519-520`); keeping it as the value, in `compare_subvi_tables`' shape, costs nothing and closes that hole.

What my citation does **not** cover: `compare_subvi_tables` is a SubVI name/path comparator, not a terminal-table helper. It needs a key/value adaptation; I am not claiming a drop-in call exists. **(b) A set-difference terminal gate does not exist anywhere in the fleet** — the only occurrences of a symmetric difference are this recipe and its own plan (`stage_d1_m3a3_rowD.py:93`, `c87b_plan.md:35`).

### B4 ALREADY MEASURED — the "ZERO `UNREAD`" half of the new D7 is green by construction on this table

`term_state` returns `UNREAD` only when a wired row carries any error, or when `conn_err`/`wire_err` carry something **other than 1055** (`build_d1_m3a1.py:524-534`). On this node's table every bare row prints `errs=[0, 0, 0, 1055]` — `conn_err` **0** — e.g. `build_d1_m3a3b_rowD.log:27`, `:33`, and all six rows of the junk node at `:101-106`, while `gscript.py:914` documents bare as *"conn_err/wire_err carry 1055"*. The `ConnErr` label is present in `tools/bench/opnodeterms_labels.json:7`, so this is a real read of 0, not the missing-label default at `gscript.py:947-953`.

This was measured and recorded **before** this plan was written, unacted: *"the column `term_state` needs to detect UNREAD — `conn_err` — reads 0 on all 120 printed rows, including every bare one … One of the four error columns printed as evidence may not be a measurement"* (`archive/peer/2026-09-22-c87-rowd-d7-termcount.md:131`, carried into the disposition at `:196-198`).

So the plan's offline check (*"0 UNREAD on each side"*, `c87b_plan.md:40-41`) is not a prediction that could have come out otherwise on this table — it is the same *"green by construction"* objection the review raised against the old D7's `total` half, re-introduced as the new gate's second half. The **symmetric-difference half is genuinely new and is a real prediction**; only the UNREAD half is vacuous here.

